:"கருங்கால்","parts":[{"text":"கருங்கால்","lemma":"கருங்கால்","gloss":"black-trunked"}],"gloss":"black-trunked","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"வேங்கை","parts":[{"text":"வேங்கை","lemma":"vēṅkai","gloss":"Kino tree"}],"gloss":"Vēṅkai tree"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"மேக்கெழு","parts":[{"text":"மேக்கு","lemma":"mēkku","gloss":"upward"},{"text":"எழு","lemma":"eḻu","gloss":"rising"}],"gloss":"rising upward"},{"surface":"பெருஞ்சினை","parts":[{"text":"பெருஞ்சினை","lemma":"பெருஞ்சினை","gloss":"large branch"}],"gloss":"large branch","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"இருந்த","parts":[{"text":"இருந்த","lemma":"irunta","gloss":"perched / sat"}],"gloss":"perched"},{"surface":"தோகை","parts":[{"text":"தோகை","lemma":"tōkai","gloss":"peacock"}],"gloss":"peacock"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பூக்கொய்","parts":[{"text":"பூக்கொய்","lemma":"பூக்கொய்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"மகளிரிற்","parts":[{"text":"மகளிரிற்","lemma":"மகளிரிற்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"றோன்று","parts":[{"text":"றோன்று","lemma":"றோன்று","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"நாடன்","parts":[{"text":"நாடன்","lemma":"நாடன்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true}],"as_printed":true},{"words":[{"surface":"தகாஅன்","parts":[{"text":"தகாஅன்","lemma":"takāaṉ","gloss":"unworthy man"}],"gloss":"unworthy man"},{"surface":"போல","parts":[{"text":"போல","lemma":"pōla","gloss":"like"}],"gloss":"like"},{"surface":"தான்","parts":[{"text":"தான்","lemma":"tāṉ","gloss":"himself"}],"gloss":"himself"},{"surface":"தீது","parts":[{"text":"தீது","lemma":"tītu","gloss":"evil / bad"}],"gloss":"evil"},{"surface":"மொழியினும்","parts":[{"text":"மொழி","lemma":"moḻi","gloss":"speak"},{"text":"இனும்","lemma":"iṉum","gloss":"even if"}],"gloss":"even if he speaks"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"தன்கண்","parts":[{"text":"தன்","lemma":"taṉ","gloss":"one's own"},{"text":"கண்","lemma":"kaṇ","gloss":"eye"}],"gloss":"one's own eye"},{"surface":"கண்டது","parts":[{"text":"கண்டது","lemma":"கண்டது","gloss":"what was seen"}],"gloss":"what was seen","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"பொய்க்குவது","parts":[{"text":"பொய்","lemma":"poy","gloss":"lie"},{"text":"குவது","lemma":"kuvatu","gloss":"that which will"}],"gloss":"that which will lie"},{"surface":"அன்றே","parts":[{"text":"அன்று","lemma":"aṉṟu","gloss":"not so"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"indeed / emphasis"}],"gloss":"is it not?"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"தேக்கொக்கு","parts":[{"text":"தேக்கொக்கு","lemma":"தேக்கொக்கு","gloss":"sweet tender mango"}],"gloss":"sweet tender mango","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"அருந்தும்","parts":[{"text":"அருந்து","lemma":"aruntu","gloss":"eat"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"relative participle suffix"}],"gloss":"eating"},{"surface":"முள்ளெயிற்று","parts":[{"text":"முள்ளெயிற்று","lemma":"முள்ளெயிற்று","gloss":"having sharp teeth"}],"gloss":"having sharp teeth","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"துவர்வாய்","parts":[{"text":"துவர்","lemma":"tuvar","gloss":"red / coral"},{"text":"வாய்","lemma":"vāy","gloss":"mouth"}],"gloss":"red mouth"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"வரை","parts":[{"text":"வரை","lemma":"varai","gloss":"mountain"}],"gloss":"mountain"},{"surface":"ஆடு","parts":[{"text":"ஆடு","lemma":"āṭu","gloss":"roaming / playing"}],"gloss":"roaming"},{"surface":"வன்பறழ்","parts":[{"text":"வன்பறழ்","lemma":"வன்பறழ்","gloss":"strong young cub"}],"gloss":"strong young cub","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"தந்தை","parts":[{"text":"தந்தை","lemma":"tantai","gloss":"father"}],"gloss":"father"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"கடுவனும்","parts":[{"text":"கடுவன்","lemma":"kaṭuvaṉ","gloss":"male monkey"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"also"}],"gloss":"the male monkey too"},{"surface":"அறியும்","parts":[{"text":"அறி","lemma":"aṟi","gloss":"know"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"habitual future"}],"gloss":"knows"},{"surface":"அ","parts":[{"text":"அ","lemma":"a","gloss":"that"}],"gloss":"that"},{"surface":"கொடியோனையே","parts":[{"text":"கொடியோனையே","lemma":"கொடியோனையே","gloss":"the cruel man indeed"}],"gloss":"the cruel man indeed","split_unverified":true}]}],"literal":"Buds-ceasing blossomed black-trunked Vēṅkai / upward-rising large branch perched peacock / flower-plucking women-like appearing lord of the land / unworthy man like himself evil even if he speaks / one's own eye saw will lie is it not? / sweet tender mango eating sharp-toothed red-mouthed / mountain-roaming strong-cub's father / male monkey also knows that cruel man indeed.","translation":"Even if the lord of the land—where a peacock perched on a high, rising branch of a black-trunked Vēṅkai tree in full bloom looks like a woman plucking flowers—speaks untruths like an unworthy man, can what our own eyes have seen turn out to be a lie? Even the male monkey, the father of the strong little cub with sharp teeth and a red mouth that eats sweet tender mangoes as it roams the mountains, knows that cruel man.","modern":"அரும்புகள் இல்லாமல் முழுமையாக மலர்ந்த கரிய அடிமரத்தைக் கொண்ட வேங்கை மரத்தின் மேல்நோக்கி வளர்ந்த பெரிய கிளையில் அமர்ந்திருக்கும் மயில், பூக்களைப் பறிக்கும் பெண்களைப் போலத் தோன்றும் நாட்டை உடையவன் நம் தலைவன். அவன் தகுதியில்லாதவனைப் போலத் தனக்குத் தீமை தரும் பொய்களைப் பேசினாலும், நம் கண்கள் நேரில் கண்ட உண்மை பொய்யாகிவிடுமா? மலைகளில் திரியும், கூர்மையான பற்களையும் சிவந்த வாயையும் கொண்டு இனிமையான மாம்பழங்களை உண்ணும் வலிமையான குட்டியின் தந்தையாகிய ஆண் குரங்கும் அந்த இரக்கமற்ற தலைவனைப் பற்றி நன்கு அறியும்.","explanation":"The speaker is the heroine's friend (tōḻi) speaking to the heroine (or to the hero within earshot) to reassure her of the hero's love and the truth of their union. The poem belongs to the Kuriñci (mountainous) landscape, characterized by the Vēṅkai tree, peacocks, and monkeys. The friend points out that even if the hero tries to deny their relationship or speaks words that seem distant, the truth of their secret meetings cannot be hidden. She uses the vivid image of a peacock on a Vēṅkai branch looking like a flower-plucking woman, and a male monkey witnessing their love. The key words are 'வேங்கை' (Vēṅkai tree), 'தோகை' (peacock), 'கண்டது' (what was seen), and 'கடுவனும் அறியும்' (even the male monkey knows), emphasizing that nature itself stands witness to their bond.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}